 r←GetInstallInfo packageID
⍝ Returns the install command for the top of a package page, as a vector of character vectors.
⍝ `packageID` names a major version line, like "aplteam-Cider-0", or a package without any
⍝ version at all: either way the command resolves to the newest release, which is what one
⍝ wants to install.
⍝ "[tatin]" is the alias of the Registry the package is to come from, and /path/ is what the
⍝ user has to replace: the command is an example to copy, not one to run blind.
⍝ `GetJavaScriptForCopyButton` puts a copy button next to the command.
 r←⊂'<div class="install">'
 r,←⊂'<p class="install-label">Install</p>'
 r,←⊂'<div class="install-cmd-box"><code id="install-cmd">]TATIN.InstallPackages [tatin]',(EscapeSpecialChars packageID),' /path/</code></div>'
 r,←⊂'</div>'
⍝Done
